      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5b9f6c965a3e1a116727dfa8|full_name}: \nYou can. Its tricky but you can. You'll have to set up colliders with send/receive signals that trigger depending on which bone/hand enters them and then enables them to be grabbed. However this does not solve potential edge cases where both hands would be near a collider possibly enabling both hands to grab something (such as when holding hands close to each other enabling each others colliders which in turn allows both hands to grab both the other and themselves)",
